your talents so early in the game.

247
00:14:49,613 --> 00:14:52,573
A mistake that will cost you dearly.

248
00:14:55,653 --> 00:14:57,713
Let's resume the game, Jotaro.

249
00:15:03,673 --> 00:15:04,753
Yes, he did it!

250
00:15:05,413 --> 00:15:06,573
That's my boy!

251
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:09,167
Another home run right out of the park!

252
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:10,833
Talk about a comeback!

253
00:15:11,233 --> 00:15:12,950
Four runs in the first inning!

254
00:15:13,033 --> 00:15:16,033
Looks like you've got this
game in the bag, Jotaro!

255
00:15:16,193 --> 00:15:19,017
Keep it up, and we'll be
out of here in no time!

256
00:15:19,893 --> 00:15:24,693
Hey, Darby, you'll just ignore me, but
I'll say it anyway because I'm a nice guy.

257
00:15:25,053 --> 00:15:26,347
I'm giving you an out.

258
00:15:26,433 --> 00:15:30,770
All you have to do is return Kakyoin's soul
and take us to Dio of your own volition.

259
00:15:30,853 --> 00:15:33,573
If you cooperate, no harm will befall you!

260
00:15:38,833 --> 00:15:39,663
Huh?

261
00:15:40,453 --> 00:15:43,673
For all his faults, my
brother was a master gambler.

262
00:15:43,873 --> 00:15:46,226
He made conning people into an art form.

263
00:15:47,253 --> 00:15:50,590
You'd think his younger brother
would be perfect to practice on.

264
00:15:50,673 --> 00:15:51,913
But you'd be wrong.

265
00:15:52,233 --> 00:15:54,730
He never asked me to
play one game of poker.

266
00:15:54,813 --> 00:15:58,754
No, I was never asked to play any
games of the gambling persuasion.

267
00:15:58,893 --> 00:16:00,313
Any guesses why?

268
00:16:02,513 --> 00:16:03,733
When I was 15,

269
00:16:04,033 --> 00:16:07,990
I caught my brother putting his
oh-so-predictable moves on my girlfriend.

270
00:16:08,073 --> 00:16:11,270
He was 10 years older, but
I beat him to a bloody pulp.

271
00:16:11,353 --> 00:16:15,093
I broke his ribs and proceeded
to kick him until he spat blood.

272
00:16:15,413 --> 00:16:18,730
The last thing my brother said
to me was how sorry he was.

273
00:16:18,813 --> 00:16:20,373
Any idea why?

274
00:16:20,713 --> 00:16:23,130
Would you please cut to the chase already?

275
00:16:23,213 --> 00:16:24,043
Even as kids,

276
00:16:24,213 --> 00:16:25,950
my brother had the good sense to realize

277
00:16:26,033 --> 00:16:28,210
that he'd never have
what it took to beat me.

278
00:16:28,293 --> 00:16:31,653
The reason for that is about
to become abundantly clear.

279
00:16:32,773 --> 00:16:37,893
At this moment, you have a false sense of
confidence due to the home run you hit.

280
00:16:38,173 --> 00:16:42,530
But deep down, you feel a sense of
unease, not unlike what my brother felt.

281
00:16:42,613 --> 00:16:45,378
My prowess is beginning
to worry you, isn't it?

282
00:16:45,593 --> 00:16:49,710
Right now, you're coming to a daunting
conclusion about the game's outcome,

283
00:16:49,793 --> 00:16:50,911
aren't you, Jotaro?

284
00:16:51,253 --> 00:16:53,371
What the hell are you talking about?

285
00:16:55,313 --> 00:16:59,570
Changing pictures number 15
is out and number 77 is in.

286
00:16:59,653 --> 00:17:05,250
77 is a power pitcher with a max pitch
speed of 165 kilometers per hour.

287
00:17:05,333 --> 00:17:11,890
Also I'll tell you the pitch
I'll throw number 77 will

288
00:17:11,973 --> 00:17:15,090
throw a forkball and he'll
throw it right down the middle.

289
00:17:15,173 --> 00:17:19,230
What the hell why would he
declare what he's Throwing

290
00:17:19,313 --> 00:17:22,290
a fork ball is about to
come barreling down center,

291
00:17:22,373 --> 00:17:24,197
but will you believe me or not?

292
00:17:24,673 --> 00:17:27,530
Jotaro he's just spouting
nonsense to shake your confidence

293
00:17:27,613 --> 00:17:30,593
do yourself a favor and
ignore everything he says.

294
00:17:31,193 --> 00:17:32,673
Throw it Darby!

295
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:35,793
Will you believe or will you doubt?

296
00:17:41,733 --> 00:17:42,833
I knew it.

297
00:17:42,933 --> 00:17:45,490
It's a fastball, and
it's coming right at you.

298
00:17:45,573 --> 00:17:48,397
Let's see is the ball
going to change direction?

299
00:17:48,773 --> 00:17:50,714
The suspense is driving me crazy!

300
00:17:51,953 --> 00:17:53,073
You swung!

301
00:17:53,293 --> 00:17:55,730
You bought his act and
bet on the forkball!

302
00:17:55,813 --> 00:17:56,813
It's still going!

303
00:17:57,093 --> 00:17:58,913
It actually is a fastball!

304
00:17:59,913 --> 00:18:02,353
Oh great, he hit the bottom of the ball!

305
00:18:04,413 --> 00:18:05,243
Out!

306
00:18:05,653 --> 00:18:07,893
First inning, three outs change!

307
00:18:12,453 --> 00:18:13,913
Idiot, how could you?

308
00:18:14,193 --> 00:18:16,330
Leave it to a rookie
for something like that!

309
00:18:16,413 --> 00:18:18,953
I can't believe you swung for a forkball!

310
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:20,803
Hmph.

311
00:18:21,233 --> 00:18:22,063
No.

312
00:18:22,146 --> 00:18:26,230
He had already seen through me and knew
I would swing expecting a forkball.

313
00:18:26,313 --> 00:18:28,413
So we switched it up to a fastball.

314
00:18:28,693 --> 00:18:30,281
But he has a point, though.

315
00:18:30,593 --> 00:18:34,050
Something's been gnawing at me ever
since we stepped foot in this mansion.

316
00:18:34,133 --> 00:18:35,293
I'm not sure how.

317
00:18:35,553 --> 00:18:39,630
But he knew Star Platinum would throw
a right punch in our earlier skirmish.

318
00:18:39,713 --> 00:18:40,543
What?

319
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:41,783
Impossible!

320
00:18:41,953 --> 00:18:44,110
Are you trying to tell me
that he can read your mind?

321
00:18:44,193 --> 00:18:46,773
No offense, Jotaro, but that's crazy talk.

322
00:18:48,193 --> 00:18:49,781
Oh, would you look at that.

323
00:18:49,953 --> 00:18:51,213
It's my turn at bat.

324
00:19:01,113 --> 00:19:02,937
This is going to be a home run.

325
00:19:03,713 --> 00:19:08,478
Keep your eye on the birdie, as I'll be
hitting it into the left field bleachers.

326
00:19:09,693 --> 00:19:12,190
Old man, are you absolutely sure?

327
00:19:12,273 --> 00:19:14,270
The game and console
haven't been tampered with.

328
00:19:14,353 --> 00:19:17,290
Yeah, I'm positive it's
clean and that's not all.

329
00:19:17,373 --> 00:19:19,890
I haven't seen him make a
single funny move either.

330
00:19:19,973 --> 00:19:22,950
Then a secret weapon has
to be that stand of his.

331
00:19:23,033 --> 00:19:26,850
His stand doesn't just take souls
it must have some other ability.

332
00:19:26,933 --> 00:19:30,993
This will be my target.

333
00:19:34,933 --> 00:19:36,690
Now I'll get to the bottom of this.

334
00:19:36,773 --> 00:19:38,830
Has he lost his mind?

335
00:19:38,913 --> 00:19:43,330
He's going to try to hit the better on
purpose and where might you be aiming?

336
00:19:43,413 --> 00:19:48,490
Now Jotaro, an inside pitch
will you throw it high or low?

337
00:19:48,573 --> 00:19:52,410
Perhaps or maybe you're planning
some kind of underhanded trick?

338
00:19:52,493 --> 00:19:53,433
Well.

339
00:20:01,873 --> 00:20:05,253
What the people back with
Jotaro through the ball?

340
00:20:09,353 --> 00:20:11,013
He predicted it.

341
00:20:11,473 --> 00:20:14,793
He knew exactly what
would happen. But how?

342
00:20:15,093 --> 00:20:19,130
There's no way he could have seen that
pitch coming unless he read Jotaro's mind.

343
00:20:19,213 --> 00:20:20,073
Home run!

344
00:20:23,753 --> 00:20:24,873
That's one run.

345
00:20:26,253 --> 00:20:27,370
Damn this bastard.

346
00:20:27,453 --> 00:20:29,850
We faced all kinds of
opponents on this journey,

347
00:20:29,933 --> 00:20:31,770
but never one who could read our minds.

348
00:20:31,853 --> 00:20:36,130
If you really can read minds, then it
doesn't matter how clever we think we are.

349
00:20:36,213 --> 00:20:38,742
We won't stand a
snowball's chance in hell!

350
00:20:39,253 --> 00:20:41,194
Jotaro, what are you going to do?

351
00:20:54,273 --> 00:20:55,333
Why that?

352
00:20:55,633 --> 00:20:58,221
Damn, the punk's declaring
another home run!

353
00:20:58,493 --> 00:20:59,433
Let's see.

354
00:20:59,813 --> 00:21:01,173
An outside pitch?

355
00:21:02,293 --> 00:21:06,713
Or maybe you're going to aim low, or
something in the vein of a fastball.

356
00:21:18,273 --> 00:21:19,313
Home run!

357
00:21:20,553 --> 00:21:21,693
Four to two.

358
00:21:24,013 --> 00:21:24,843
Damn!

359
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:27,870
A person's body language and
the surrounding environment go

360
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,670
a long way toward helping
predict an opponent's next move.

361
00:21:30,753 --> 00:21:33,870
But there's no way to do
it perfectly and yet his

362
00:21:33,953 --> 00:21:37,890
stand predicts Jotaro's pitch
with 100 % accuracy and!

363
00:21:37,973 --> 00:21:39,797
Technically, he's not cheating?

364
00:21:41,473 --> 00:21:42,553
Another home run!

365
00:21:42,793 --> 00:21:43,853
It's 4-3!

366
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:47,650
How are we supposed to stop
him from reading our minds?

367
00:21:47,733 --> 00:21:48,563
How?

368
00:21:52,213 --> 00:21:56,053
At this rate, I'll be in the
lead in no time. Now what's next?

369
00:21:56,293 --> 00:22:00,293
An inside pitch, a fastball, a
high pitch, or maybe a curveball?

370
00:22:00,753 --> 00:22:02,047
What's up your sleeve?

371
00:22:04,713 --> 00:22:05,543
Huh?

372
00:22:06,633 --> 00:22:07,513
Your hat.

373
00:22:08,313 --> 00:22:09,153
You idiot.

374
00:22:09,493 --> 00:22:13,434
Do you honestly take me for a cheat
like my ne 'er-do-well brother?

375
00:22:13,613 --> 00:22:15,190
Jotaro, you've got it wrong.

376
00:22:15,273 --> 00:22:16,920
Hiding your face is useless.

377
00:22:17,033 --> 00:22:18,370
I don't know what he's doing,

378
00:22:18,453 --> 00:22:21,410
but he's not watching the reflection
of the screen in your eyes.

379
00:22:21,493 --> 00:22:23,770
I get that it's hard not to go there now,

380
00:22:23,853 --> 00:22:27,870
but there's no way he can see what you're
pressing or what pitch you're choosing.

381
00:22:27,953 --> 00:22:30,050
Trust me, I've been watching
him the entire time.

382
00:22:30,133 --> 00:22:32,309
That's not what's been going on here.

383
00:22:32,453 --> 00:22:34,650
I only took off my hat
because I'm sweating.

384
00:22:34,733 --> 00:22:35,873
No other reason.

385
00:22:36,213 --> 00:22:39,213
Could you throw your next
pitch sometime this year?

386
00:22:40,653 --> 00:22:43,173
But I'm not going to be sweating anymore.

387
00:22:43,553 --> 00:22:45,313
I'll tell you my next pitch.

388
00:22:46,373 --> 00:22:48,973
I'm throwing a high outside fastball.

389
00:22:49,433 --> 00:22:51,413
You're joking! Totoro!

390
00:22:51,733 --> 00:22:54,145
Do you hear what you're saying right now?

391
00:22:54,553 --> 00:22:55,730
Of course I do.

392
00:22:55,813 --> 00:22:57,950
Finally starting to lose
your hearing, old man.

393
00:22:58,033 --> 00:23:00,653
Obviously, I just told him my next pitch.

394
00:23:00,893 --> 00:23:02,633
A high outside fastball.

395
00:23:02,793 --> 00:23:04,264
That's how I'm gonna win.

396
00:23:08,393 --> 00:23:09,513
Huh? Jotaro?

397
00:23:13,453 --> 00:23:14,913
Will you believe me?

398
00:23:15,233 --> 00:23:16,593
Or will you doubt me?

399
00:23:19,513 --> 00:23:20,343
Hmph.

400
00:23:20,426 --> 00:23:21,897
You're not too bright, are you?

401
00:23:28,413 --> 00:23:30,470
Do you hear what you're saying right now?

402
00:23:30,553 --> 00:23:32,390
Obviously, I just told him my next pitch.

403
00:23:32,473 --> 00:23:33,303
What the hell?

404
00:23:33,386 --> 00:23:34,550
He's telling the truth!

405
00:23:34,633 --> 00:23:35,463
Yes.

406
00:23:35,546 --> 00:23:36,430
You tampered with the console!

407
00:23:36,513 --> 00:23:37,343
No!

408
00:23:37,426 --> 00:23:39,050
It must have something to
do with that hat of yours!

409
00:23:39,133 --> 00:23:42,780
This is just a dance of deception
where the loser cries first.
